    {
      "page_title": "Visibility Map & Two-Pass VACUUM",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Vacuum Is A Feature"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A fresh visibility map is what enables index-only scans",
            "Vacuum is a performance feature, not just cleanup",
            "Tune it like you tune indexes"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Visibility Map Bits"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Bit",
            "Means",
            "Enables"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "all-visible",
              "no dead tuples",
              "==index-only scans=="
            ],
            [
              "all-frozen",
              "nothing to freeze",
              "aggressive scan skips page"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Two-Pass VACUUM"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Scan heap, collect dead TIDs",
            "Remove those TIDs from **every** index",
            "Return to heap, free the line pointers",
            "Update the free space map and visibility map"
          ],
          "style": "number"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "EXPLAIN (ANALYZE)",
            "SELECT id FROM t WHERE id < 100;",
            "-- Heap Fetches: 0 = fresh vm"
          ],
          "note": "high heap fetches means vacuum lags"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Append-Only Tables",
          "text": "They never get dead tuples, so only the PG13+ insert threshold keeps their ==visibility map== fresh."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "The Whole Chain: Queue Tables & HOT Health",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Whole Chain"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "xmin/xmax + snapshot",
              "visibility",
              "horizon + time",
              "dead tuples",
              "no vacuum",
              "bloat + wraparound"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Daily Health Set",
          "items": [
            "`n_dead_tup` / `n_live_tup` ratio",
            "`age(datfrozenxid)` per database",
            "Oldest `xact_start` in `pg_stat_activity`",
            "`last_autovacuum` per hot table"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Worked Example: Queue Table"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Symptom: 2M live rows, 40 GB on disk",
            "Cause: default 0.2 scale factor, so cleanup waits",
            "Second cause: an index on `status`, so no HOT updates",
            "Fix 1: per-table scale factor at 0.01",
            "Fix 2: `fillfactor = 85` to keep updates on-page",
            "Fix 3: move `status` churn out of the indexed path"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "SELECT relname, n_dead_tup, n_live_tup,",
            "       last_autovacuum",
            "FROM pg_stat_user_tables",
            "ORDER BY n_dead_tup DESC;"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Check HOT Health"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "SELECT relname, n_tup_upd,",
            "       n_tup_hot_upd",
            "FROM pg_stat_user_tables",
            "ORDER BY n_tup_upd DESC;"
          ],
          "note": "ratio near 0 = HOT is dead"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Indexing `last_seen_at` kills HOT for the whole table",
            "`fillfactor` 100 on an update-heavy table",
            "Updates that keep changing an indexed column"
          ],
          "style": "cross"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Write Amplification"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Update",
            "Heap",
            "Index writes"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "HOT",
              "1",
              "**0**"
            ],
            [
              "non-HOT, 6 idx",
              "1",
              "6"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Every UPDATE rewrites the ==whole row==",
            "Unchanged TOAST values reuse the same pointer",
            "PG16+: BRIN-covered column changes stay HOT"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Fillfactor Trade-off",
          "items": [
            "80-90 leaves room for on-page versions",
            "Costs more pages for the same live rows",
            "Sequential scans read more"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Fix Pattern",
          "text": "Move the churning column into a narrow side table with no indexes on it."
        }
      ]
