    "text": "Part 2 of POSTGRES INTERNALS. Your UPDATE didn't change that row — it wrote a whole new copy and left the old one on disk. That one design choice explains free rollbacks, table bloat, autovacuum, and the 4.2-billion transaction cliff, all at once. 10 pages on tuple headers, snapshots, HOT updates, and the monitoring queries that catch a frozen horizon before it stops your writes.",
